+Not blocked. Implemented, verified, committed on `task/T-102`. This is the
+attempt-2 handoff; attempt 1 failed the guard with exit 6 — root cause and fix
+in the next section.
+
+## Retry: guard exit 6 — root cause and fix
+
+Attempt 1's handoff prose contained the literal guard-forbidden marker strings
+(the exact tokens from `cmd/harness/scan.go`'s scan list) inside the sentence
+that asserted their absence — a self-referential false positive.
+
+`checkMarkers` (guard check 5) scans **added lines of `git diff main...HEAD`**
+and exempts only `*_test.go`, `acceptance/**` and `harness/selftest/**`. It
+does NOT exempt `harness/handoffs/**`, so handoff prose is scanned like code.
+The offending line was in the old "notes" section: the sentence asserting
+rule-9 compliance quoted the scanned marker tokens themselves. Fix: reworded
+the handoff to describe rule-9 compliance without reproducing any scanned
+token, then recommitted. No production or test file was ever affected —
+`internal/web/csrf.go` (the only non-test file in this task's diff besides the
+handoff) is marker-clean by inspection and by the same scan.
+
+Lesson for future handoff authors: never quote the scan list verbatim in
+`harness/handoffs/**`; the guard reads your prose as if it were code.
